# BUILD ARTIFACTS, for any game with a build.sh.
#
# A .wasc is a zip of the prebuilt engine plus the game's Lua, and main.wasm
# IS that engine -- both are reproduced by `./build.sh` in about a second and
# rebuilt from source by CI on every release. Committing them means a 3.4MB
# binary diff every time a single line of Lua changes.
#
# The card games commit their engine (main.wasm, a pinned build) but not
# their cart: a committed cart carries whatever version it was packed at, and
# a release's carts carry the release's (README, "Versions").
bowling/bowling.wasc
bowling/main.wasm
combo/combo.wasc
combo/main.wasm
eightball/eightball.wasc
eightball/main.wasm
jewels/jewels.wasc
jewels/main.wasm
minigolf/minigolf.wasc
minigolf/main.wasm
pinochle/pinochle.wasc
pinochle/main.wasm
fivecardstud/fivecardstud.wasc
jacksorbetter/jacksorbetter.wasc
sevencardstud/sevencardstud.wasc
spades/spades.wasc
fivecardstud/app/assets.index
jacksorbetter/app/assets.index
sevencardstud/app/assets.index
spades/app/assets.index
